.TH NIBWARDEND 1 2026-11-06 "nibwarden" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nibwardend \- nibwarden vault daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nibwardend
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nibwardend
keeps a Bitwarden or Vaultwarden vault for the user's session.
It serves
.BR nibwarden (1)
and nibwarden's windows on a control socket, and an SSH agent on a second socket.
.PP
It normally runs as the systemd user unit
.BR nibwardend.service ,
started the first time a nibwarden program needs it;
there is no need to start it by hand or enable the unit.
.PP
The vault is cached on disk encrypted, as the server sends it.
Unlocked keys stay in memory only, which is locked against swapping and core dumps.
The vault locks after a period without use, when the screen locks and before suspend
(see
.B [lock]
in
.BR nibwarden (1)).
When a program needs the vault while it is locked, or must be approved,
.B nibwardend
starts
.BR nibwarden\-gui (1)
to ask.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " path"
Where the session and the encrypted vault cache live.
Default:
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/nibwarden .
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
The control socket.
Default:
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nibwarden/daemon.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-agent\-socket " path"
The SSH agent socket.
Default:
.I ssh\-agent.sock
next to the control socket.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-agent
Do not serve the SSH agent.
.TP
.BI \-\-gui " path"
The
.B nibwarden\-gui
program for its windows.
Default: next to
.BR nibwardend .
.TP
.BI \-\-lock\-timeout " seconds"
Lock after this long without vault use; 0 means never.
Default: the settings file's
.BR idle_minutes ,
15 minutes.
.TP
.BI \-\-sync\-interval " seconds"
Sync this often while logged in; 0 syncs only on demand and on the server's notifications.
Default: 300.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIBWARDEN_DATA_DIR\fR, \fBNIBWARDEN_SOCKET\fR, \fBNIBWARDEN_SSH_AGENT_SOCKET\fR, \fBNIBWARDEN_GUI
Same as the options above.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR nibwardend=debug .
Logs go to stderr, which systemd puts in the journal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nibwarden/ssh\-agent.sock
The SSH agent.
To use it for every program of the session, copy
.I /usr/share/doc/nibwarden/examples/60\-nibwarden\-ssh\-agent.conf
to
.I ~/.config/environment.d/
and log in again.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/nibwardend.service
The user unit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Follow the daemon's log:
.PP
.nf
journalctl \-\-user \-u nibwardend \-f
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nibwarden (1),
.BR nibwarden\-gui (1),
.BR nibwarden\-ssh\-sign (1)
